# AI Workflow

The optional end-to-end flow is: **alternatives → planning → implementation → review → PR**.

Only use this rule when the user explicitly asks for the full workflow.

## Running the full flow

1. Read `RUNBOOK.md`.
2. Run `alternatives` and let the user pick an option.
3. Run `planning` and write the plan file to `.agents/plans/<slug>.md`.
4. Implement the plan one atomic TODO at a time.
5. Run `review-and-fix` (or `review-dont-fix` if read-only).
6. Run `pr`.

## Using subagents

Each phase should run in an independent subagent when the platform supports it. The parent acts as a thin dispatcher. Pass the plan or diff to the subagent, triage the output, and dispatch the next phase.

## Opting out

The user can stop or skip any phase. Each skill works on its own.
